=== CATEGORY_FIELDS ===
location-category fields (14 total in protomodel.Signals):

  Compounds (NOT routed; codec flattens before routing layer sees anything):
    Location              (proto 21)  -> flattens to LocationLatitude / LocationLongitude
    OriginLocation        (proto 111) -> flattens to OriginLocationLatitude / OriginLocationLongitude
    DestinationLocation   (proto 112) -> flattens to DestinationLocationLatitude / DestinationLocationLongitude

  Atomic location-category fields:
    GpsState                  -> positions   col=gps_state
    GpsHeading                -> positions   col=heading_deg
    RouteLastUpdated          -> signal_log
    RouteLine                 -> signal_log
    MilesToArrival            -> signal_log              (UnitKindDistance; SI conversion via normalize.toSI)
    MinutesToArrival          -> signal_log
    DestinationName           -> signal_log
    RouteTrafficMinutesDelay  -> signal_log
    LocatedAtHome             -> signal_log
    LocatedAtWork             -> signal_log
    LocatedAtFavorite         -> signal_log

  Codec-emitted flattened atomics (must appear in routing.yaml):
    LocationLatitude            -> positions   col=lat   (flatten group with LocationLongitude)
    LocationLongitude           -> positions   col=lng   (flatten group with LocationLatitude)
    OriginLocationLatitude      -> signal_log
    OriginLocationLongitude     -> signal_log
    DestinationLocationLatitude -> signal_log
    DestinationLocationLongitude-> signal_log

positions schema: migrations/000169_positions_si.up.sql lines 28-42 (lat / lng / heading_deg / gps_state)
location_snapshots schema: migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql lines 343-351 (place / country / region / geocoded_at — geocoder writer, no direct field route from proto)

cagg / MV references for positions columns: cagg_vehicle_daily and mv_position_hourly source lat/lng directly from positions hypertable (000175). No also_signal_log dual-write needed for any location field.

Flatten-group note: LocationLatitude/Longitude must land on the same positions row.
The YAML grammar in routing_loader.go has no flatten_group key (parser rejects unknown keys),
so the grouping is documented inline as a YAML comment. The codec emits both atomics with
a shared EmittedAt timestamp; the positions writer (added in prompt 0061) is responsible for
buffering one half until the other arrives so the pair lands atomically.
